# Law Engine public/private boundary (Live Run 1.37, Mission 25).
# This file is the real, first safeguard against accidentally publishing
# private material -- not the only one (see docs/public-private-boundary.md
# for the full policy), but the one that acts automatically.

# Private legal library material not yet cleared for public release.
# (Currently empty in practice -- this run's UCC extract is real, public-
# domain Virginia state statute text, safe to publish -- but the rule
# stays in place as a default-safe boundary for future, less-clean
# sources, e.g. copyrighted treatises, before each is individually
# reviewed and reclassified.)
library/private/

# Private case documents, personal research notes, user data.
private/
user-data/
*.secret.*

# Standard
node_modules/
.next/
apps/web/.env*.local
__pycache__/
*.pyc
